ArrayDeque is a resizable, array-based, double-ended queue implementation of Deque

Fast insert/remove from both ends using a circular buffer

Circular buffer allows efficient use of space by wrapping around when the end of the array is reached
  means only head and tail indices are maintained, no shifting of elements needed
     Think of it like a clock ⏰:
       Hand moves → numbers stay
     Pointers move → elements stay
capacity is always a power of 2 for efficient modulo operations using bitwise AND
     capacity = 2^n (e.g., 8, 16, 32, ...)
     allows for O(1) time complexity for index calculations

ArrayDeque can have 3 behaviours
| Role  | Behavior                  |
| ----- | ------------------------- |
| Queue | FIFO (First In First Out) |
| Stack | LIFO (Last In First Out)  |
| Deque | Both ends                 |

Queue operations:
Add: (Enqueue) - adds an element to the tail of the queue
  offer(e)
  offerLast(e)
  add(e)
Remove: (Dequeue) - removes an element from the head of the queue
    poll() - returns null if empty
    pollFirst()
    remove() - throws NoSuchElementException if empty
Peek: - retrieves but does not remove the head of the queue
    peek() - returns null if empty
    peekFirst()
    element() - throws NoSuchElementException if empty
Stack operations:
Push: - adds an element to the top of the stack
    push(e)
    addFirst(e)
Pop: - removes an element from the top of the stack
    pop() - throws NoSuchElementException if empty
    removeFirst() - throws NoSuchElementException if empty
Deque operations:
Add First: - adds an element to the front of the deque
    offerFirst(e)
    addFirst(e)
Add Last: - adds an element to the end of the deque
    offerLast(e)
    addLast(e)